        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "I am working on an empirical economics paper about China's urban-rural dual structure. I want a simple theoretical model explaining why children with similar ability may make different human-capital investment decisions depending on whether they are born into urban or rural households. The mechanism may involve schooling quality, household resources, education costs, migration barriers, and hukou-related access to urban labor markets. Please help me build a clean model, derive a few main propositions, and organize it into a manuscript-style theory section.",
