        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "I am working on a health economics paper about China's centralized drug procurement system. The policy lowers drug procurement prices and may reduce medical insurance spending and patient out-of-pocket costs, but very low prices may also affect firm participation and drug availability. Please help me build a simple theory model connecting centralized procurement, insurance moral hazard, patient drug demand, insurer spending, firm participation, and welfare.",
